WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — gates (45s) Narrator George

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.491
First, a computer should not take an irreversible

2
00:00:03.491 --> 00:00:07.029
action until an independent check confirms it is safe.

3
00:00:07.469 --> 00:00:10.905
Second, it should try the cheapest method first and

4
00:00:10.905 --> 00:00:14.342
wake a large AI model only when simpler tools miss.

5
00:00:14.782 --> 00:00:19.619
Third, every decision is written to a receipt with the energy it used,

6
00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.622
so anyone can audit it later.

7
00:00:22.062 --> 00:00:27.233
When software moves money, edits records, or steers machinery, saying sorry

8
00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:31.370
after a bad guess cannot undo the damage. A commit gate acts

9
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:36.817
like a physical cockpit lock that blocks unsafe switches before anything moves.

10
00:00:37.257 --> 00:00:42.929
Measured by an onboard circuit-board power sensor, checking safety rules costs about eleven

11
00:00:42.929 --> 00:00:49.225
thousand picojoules per cycle while leaving a permanent, auditable receipt for every single decision.
